meta {
  name: ENG - add tag
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/eng/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "tagNumber": "TIC-106",
    "serviceDescription": "Top temperature control",
    "unitNumber": "101",
    "classKey": "rdl:TemperatureIndicatingController"
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a tag in ENG's own vocabulary. No message is sent: edits accrue without
  ceremony, and publication is a separate deliberate act.

  Omit classKey to see the validation gate block promotion.

  No iTwinId here, so this lands in ENG's default twin. Add one to the body, or
  send x-itwin-id, to work in a specific plant - see 23 and 24. The response
  echoes the twin that was actually used.
}
